      "message": "(Qwen + QLM 5.3)\n\n### 🟠 All three commands now `fclose(stderr)` on exit\n\n`rbh-gc.c:741`, `rbh-sync.c:960`, `rbh-fsevents.c:960`:\n\n```c\nif (metadata.log_file !\u003d stdout)\n    fclose(metadata.log_file);\n```\n\nThe default changed from `stdout` to `stderr`, but the guard only excludes `stdout`. On the normal exit path of every run **without** `--log-file`, `fclose(stderr)` runs. Today nothing writes to stderr between that call and process exit, so it\u0027s latent rather than fatal — but it is now wrong, and any future `error()`/teardown print after that point would vanish. Fix: `!\u003d stdout \u0026\u0026 !\u003d stderr`.",
